1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:10,000
This is Kokoro Reader, a Chrome extension that reads any webpage aloud with natural AI speech, generated privately on your own computer.

2
00:00:11,300 --> 00:00:19,300
Install it from the release zip. Open Chrome's extensions page, turn on developer mode, and load the unpacked folder.

3
00:00:20,302 --> 00:00:29,502
The first time, Kokoro Reader downloads the eighty-nine megabyte voice model once, from a pinned version, and checks every file before using it.

4
00:00:39,298 --> 00:00:48,398
The model then starts on your device. A real test sentence decides the engine: WebAssembly, or WebGPU on supported graphics.

5
00:00:49,399 --> 00:00:52,899
Now open any article and select a paragraph.

6
00:00:53,900 --> 00:00:57,500
A small speaker appears right next to your selection.

7
00:01:04,131 --> 00:01:19,310
Tomato seedlings need steady warmth before they can be moved outdoors.

8
00:01:19,310 --> 00:01:24,010
A thin layer of compost keeps the soil moist through dry weeks.

9
00:01:24,341 --> 00:01:30,841
The floating player lets you pause, skip by sentence or paragraph, and jump anywhere in the article.

10
00:01:35,298 --> 00:01:41,298
Pick from twenty-eight English voices. Preview them, mark favorites, and switch while you listen.

11
00:01:42,297 --> 00:01:47,297
Change the speed from half to three times, instantly, with natural pitch.

12
00:01:48,295 --> 00:01:53,895
Every sentence is highlighted as it is spoken, and the page scrolls to follow along.

13
00:01:55,369 --> 00:01:58,369
To hear a whole article, click Read page.

14
00:02:04,980 --> 00:02:10,566
Slow Habits and Careful Looking

15
00:02:10,566 --> 00:02:13,677
By Jordan Ellis, published March 3

16
00:02:13,677 --> 00:02:15,113
Early Habits

17
00:02:15,413 --> 00:02:21,913
Smart Reader turns cluttered pages into a clean reading view, with a table of contents and progress.

18
00:02:22,915 --> 00:02:28,615
Save articles to Listen Later, and they play back to back, like an audiobook playlist.

19
00:02:29,615 --> 00:02:35,315
Playback keeps going while you browse other tabs, and the side panel keeps the controls close.

20
00:02:36,316 --> 00:02:42,016
You can also paste your own text, or import a text, markdown, or HTML file,

21
00:02:43,018 --> 00:02:46,218
and save the speech as a WAV file.

22
00:02:56,843 --> 00:03:03,443
Everything runs on your device. No account, no tracking, and your text never leaves your computer.

23
00:03:04,745 --> 00:03:09,745
Kokoro Reader. Natural speech for the whole web, private by design.
